            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Hark! hark! the dogs bark,</l>
               <l>The beggars are coming to town;</l>
               <l>Some in rags and some in tags,</l>
               <l>And some in a silken gown.</l>
               <l>Some gave them white bread,</l>
               <l>And some gave them brown,</l>
               <l>And some gave them a good horse-whip,</l>
               <l>And sent them out of the town.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Little Jack Horner sat in the corner,</l>
               <l>Eating a Christmas pie;</l>
               <l>He put in his thumb, and pulled out a plum,</l>
               <l>And said, oh! what a good boy am I.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>There was an old woman</l>
               <l>Lived under a hill;</l>
               <l>And if she’s not gone,</l>
               <l>She lives there still.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Diddlty, diddlty, dumpty,</l>
               <l>The cat ran up the plum tree,</l>
               <l>Give her a plum, and down she’ll come,</l>
               <l>Diddlty, diddlty, dumpty.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>We’re all jolly boys, and we're coming with a noise,</l>
               <l>Our stockings shall be made</l>
               <l>Of the finest silk,</l>
               <l>And our tails shall trail the ground.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>To market, to market, to buy a plum cake,</l>
               <l>Home again, home again, market is late;</l>
               <l>To market, to market, to buy a plum bun,</l>
               <l>Home again, home again, market is done.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Elsie Marley has grown so fine,</l>
               <l>She won’t get up to serve the swine;</l>
               <l>But lies in bed till eight or nine,</l>
               <l>And surely she does take her time.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">Daffy-down-dilly has come up to town,<lb/>In a yellow petticoat and a green gown.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Jack Sprat could eat no fat,</l>
               <l>His wife could eat no lean;</l>
               <l>And so between them both,</l>
               <l>They licked the platter clean.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Lucy Locket, lost her pocket,</l>
               <l>Kitty Fisher found it;</l>
               <l>There was not a penny in it,</l>
               <l>But a ribbon round it.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Cross Patch, lift the latch,</l>
               <l>Sit by the fire and spin;</l>
               <l>Take a cup, and drink it up,</l>
               <l>Then call your neighbours in.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Johnny shall have a new bonnet,</l>
               <l>And Johnny shall go to the fair;</l>
               <l>And Johnny shall have a blue ribbon,</l>
               <l>To tie up his bonny brown hair.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>There was a little boy and a little girl</l>
               <l>Lived in an alley;</l>
               <l>Says the little boy to the little girl,</l>
               <l>“Shall I, oh, shall I?”</l>
               <l>Says the little girl to the little boy,</l>
               <l>“What shall we do?”</l>
               <l>Says the little boy to the little girl,</l>
               <l>“I will kiss you!”</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Draw a pail of water,</l>
               <l>For my lady’s daughter;</l>
               <l>My father’s a king, and my mother’s a queen,</l>
               <l>My two little sisters are dressed in green,</l>
               <l>Stamping grass and parsley,</l>
               <l>Marigold leaves and daisies.</l>
               <l>One rush! two rush!</l>
               <l>Pray thee, fine lady, come under my bush.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Jack and Jill</l>
               <l>Went up the hill,</l>
               <l>To fetch a pail of water;</l>
               <l>Jack fell down</l>
               <l>And broke his crown,</l>
               <l>And Jill came tumbling after.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Little Bo-Peep has lost her sheep,</l>
               <l>And can’t tell where to find them;</l>
               <l>Leave them alone, and they’ll come home,</l>
               <l>And bring their tails behind them.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Polly put the kettle on,</l>
               <l>Polly put the kettle on,</l>
               <l>Polly put the kettle on,</l>
               <l>We’ll all have tea.</l>
               <l>Sukey take it off again,</l>
               <l>Sukey take it off again,</l>
               <l>Sukey take it off again,</l>
               <l>They’re all gone away.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Little Tommy Tittlemouse,</l>
               <l>Lived in a little house;</l>
               <l>He caught fishes</l>
               <l>In other men’s ditches.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Tell Tale Tit,</l>
               <l>Your tongue shall be slit;</l>
               <l>And all the dogs in the town</l>
               <l>Shall have a little bit.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Goosey, goosey, gander,</l>
               <l>Where shall I wander?</l>
               <l>Up stairs, down stairs,</l>
               <l>And in my lady’s chamber:</l>
               <l>There I met an old man,</l>
               <l>Who would not say his prayers;</l>
               <l>Take him by the left leg,</l>
               <l>Throw him down the stairs.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Willy boy, Willy boy, where are you going?</l>
               <l>I will go with you, if I may.</l>
               <l>I’m going to the meadow to see them a mowing,</l>
               <l>I’m going to help them make the hay.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Mary, Mary, quite contrary,</l>
               <l>How does your garden grow?</l>
               <l>With silver bells, and cockle shells,</l>
               <l>And cowslips all of a row.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Bonny lass, pretty lass, wilt thou be mine?</l>
               <l>Thou shall not wash dishes,</l>
               <l>Nor yet serve the swine;</l>
               <l>Thou shalt sit on a cushion, and sew a fine seam,</l>
               <l>And thou shalt eat strawberries, sugar, and cream!</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>A dillar, a dollar,</l>
               <l>A ten o’clock scholar;</l>
               <l>What makes you come so soon?</l>
               <l>You used to come at ten o’clock,</l>
               <l>But now you come at noon!</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Little Betty Blue,</l>
               <l>Lost her holiday shoe.</l>
               <l>What will poor Betty do?</l>
               <l>Why, give her another,</l>
               <l>To match the other,</l>
               <l>And then she will walk in two.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Billy boy blue, come blow me your horn,</l>
               <l>The sheep’s in the meadow, the cow’s in the corn;</l>
               <l>Is that the way you mind your sheep,</l>
               <l>Under the haycock fast asleep!</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Girls and boys come out to play,</l>
               <l>The moon it shines as bright as day;</l>
               <l>Leave your supper, and leave your sleep,</l>
               <l>And come to your playmates in the street;</l>
               <l>Come with a whoop, come with a call,</l>
               <l>Come with a good will, or come not at all;</l>
               <l>Up the ladder and down the wall,</l>
               <l>A halfpenny loaf will serve us all.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Here am I, little jumping Joan,</l>
               <l>When nobody’s with me,</l>
               <l>I’m always alone.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Ride a cock-horse,</l>
               <l>To Banbury-cross,</l>
               <l>To see little Johnny</l>
               <l>Get on a white horse.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Rock-a-bye baby,</l>
               <l>Thy cradle is green;</l>
               <l>Father’s a nobleman,</l>
               <l>Mother’s a queen.</l>
               <l>And Betty’s a lady,</l>
               <l>And wears a gold ring;</l>
               <l>And Johnny’s a drummer,</l>
               <l>And drums for the king.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Little Tom Tucker,</l>
               <l>He sang for his supper.</l>
               <l>What did he sing for?</l>
               <l>Why, white bread and butter.</l>
               <l>How can I cut it without a knife?</l>
               <l>How can I marry without a wife?</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Little Miss Muffet,</l>
               <l>Sat on a tuffet,</l>
               <l>Eating some curds and whey;</l>
               <l>There came a great spider,</l>
               <l>And sat down beside her,</l>
               <l>And frightened Miss Muffet away.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">Humpty Dumpty sat on a wall,<lb/>Humpty Dumpty had a great fall.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">See-Saw-Jack in the hedge,<lb/>Which is the way to London Bridge?</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Little lad, little lad,</l>
               <l>Where wast thou born?</l>
               <l>Far off in Lancashire,</l>
               <l>Under a thorn;</l>
               <l>Where they sup sour milk</l>
               <l>From a ram’s horn.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>As I was going up Pippin Hill,</l>
               <l>Pippin Hill was dirty;</l>
               <l>There I met a sweet pretty lass,</l>
               <l>And she dropped me a curtsey.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Little maid, little maid,</l>
               <l>Whither goest thou?</l>
               <l>Down in the meadow</l>
               <l>To milk my cow.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>My mother, and your mother,</l>
               <l>Went over the way;</l>
               <l>Said my mother, to your mother,</l>
               <l>“It’s chop-a-nose day.”</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>All around the green gravel,</l>
               <l>The grass grows so green,</l>
               <l>And all the pretty maids are fit to be seen;</l>
               <l>Wash them in milk,</l>
               <l>Dress them in silk,</l>
               <l>And the first to go down shall be married.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">One foot up, the other foot down,<lb/>That’s the way to London town.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Georgie Peorgie, pudding and pie,</l>
               <l>Kissed the girls and made them cry;</l>
               <l>When the girls begin to play,</l>
               <l>Georgie Peorgie runs away.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>As Tommy Snooks, and Bessie Brooks</l>
               <l>Were walking out one Sunday;</l>
               <l>Says Tommy Snooks to Bessie Brooks,</l>
               <l>“To-morrow—will be Monday.”</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Tom, Tom, the piper’s son,</l>
               <l>He learnt to play when he was young,</l>
               <l>He with his pipe made such a noise,</l>
               <l>That he pleased all the girls and boys.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <lg>
               <l>Ring-a-ring-a-roses,</l>
               <l>A pocket full of posies;</l>
               <l>Hush! hush! hush! hush!</l>
               <l>We’re all tumbled down.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
